 < picture.gif | pnmscale 0.5 | ppmtopgm > small.pgmKept in their own directory because 169 near-identically named converters in/dd/CMDS would bury everything else.TESTED 2026-08-27 against real image data, not merely started:tools/datatests/netpbm.cases converts out of PNM and back and requires thedifference to be zero pixel for pixel.  Fifteen formats round-trip exactly --xbm, icon, ybm, g3, macp, cmuwm, mgr, atk, gem, gif, pcx, bmp, tga, sgi,rast, ilbm, xpm and rgb3.  Two findings came out of it:  NINE PROGRAMS DIED WITH `**** Stack Overflow ****' and are FIXED.  Every  netpbm module shipped with the same M$Stack of 3072 and these nine want  more; they now ask for 64k.  Five went from broken to working -- ppmnorm,  pnmtosir, ppmtoxpm, xpmtoppm and pbmtext -- and four that were being handed  a format they do not read now print their own diagnostic instead of  crashing: fstopgm, hipstopgm, imgtoppm, xvminitoppm.  pnmtosir/sirtopnm DO NOT ROUND-TRIP, and this is not fixed.  The image  comes back the right size with its channels ROTATED over the first half of  the pixels: a solid red 4x1 returns as green, green, red, red.  Which of  the pair is at fault cannot be told here -- there is no reference SIR file  to test either one against alone.  Use another format.THREE MORE, measured 2026-09-01 (tools/datatests/netpbm4.cases):  ppmtopict/picttoppm ROUND-TRIP EXACTLY -- add PICT to the list above.  picttoppm warns `can't load font directory' and converts anyway.  ppmtoyuvsplit/yuvsplittoppm round-trip the SIZE and not the pixels, and  that is the format rather than a fault: 4:2:0 chroma subsampling keeps one  luma byte per pixel and one chroma pair per 2x2 block, so a 32x16 image  gives .Y = 512 bytes and .U = .V = 128.  ppmtoyuvsplit takes a BASENAME  and writes three files beside the DATA directory, not to standard output.  sputoppm DOES NOT NOTICE what it is given.  Where nineteen other `into  PNM' converters answer `not a <format> file' for something that is not  theirs, sputoppm reads any bytes as an Atari Spectrum 512 picture and  writes a 320x200 PPM -- the format is a fixed size with no magic number  to check.  imgtoppm says nothing at all and writes nothing.  pbmtobbnbg ENDS THE EMULATOR SESSION, given a valid PBM this disk's own  pgmtopbm made.  Nothing written, nothing said.  Measured twice.  INTO the PNM formats (53)  asciitopgm     atktopbm       bioradtopgm    bmptoppm  brushtopbm     cmuwmtopbm     fitstopnm      fstopgm  g3topbm        gemtopbm       giftopnm       gouldtoppm  hipstopgm      hpcdtoppm      icontopbm      ilbmtoppm  imgtoppm       lispmtopgm     macptopbm      mgrtopbm  mtvtoppm       pbmtopgm       pcxtoppm       pgmtopbm  pgmtoppm       pi1toppm       pi3topbm       picttoppm  pjtoppm        pktopbm        ppmtopgm       psidtopgm  qrttoppm       rasttopnm      rawtopgm       rawtoppm  rgb3toppm      sgitopnm       sirtopnm       sldtoppm  spctoppm       spottopgm      sputoppm       tgatoppm  xbmtopbm       ximtoppm       xpmtoppm       xvminitoppm  xwdtopnm       ybmtopbm       yuvsplittoppm  yuvtoppm  zeisstopnm     Zeiss confocal image to PNM  OUT OF the PNM formats (58)  pbmto10x       pbmto4425      pbmtoascii     pbmtoatk  pbmtobbnbg     pbmtocmuwm     pbmtoepsi      pbmtoepson  pbmtog3        pbmtogem       pbmtogo        pbmtoicon  pbmtolj        pbmtoln03      pbmtolps       pbmtomacp  pbmtomgr       pbmtopgm       pbmtopi3       pbmtopk  pbmtoplot      pbmtoptx       pbmtox10bm     pbmtoxbm  pbmtoybm       pbmtozinc      pgmtofs        pgmtolispm  pgmtopbm       pgmtoppm       pnmtoddif      pnmtofits  pnmtops        pnmtorast      pnmtosgi       pnmtosir  pnmtoxwd       ppmtoacad      ppmtobmp       ppmtogif  ppmtoicr       ppmtoilbm      ppmtomap       ppmtomitsu  ppmtopcx       ppmtopgm       ppmtopi1       ppmtopict  ppmtopj        ppmtopjxl      ppmtopuzz      ppmtorgb3  ppmtosixel     ppmtotga       ppmtoui